From 3416a24527ddc7e9915d2ec3d9072e30cd3e7dfd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:41:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] opstack: execute Base chains with the maintained Base EVM
 over proof-backed state

Base mainnet/Sepolia run base/base v1.5.1 base-common-evm (BaseEvmFactory,
BaseSpecId by timestamp from base-common-chains, Base precompile sets incl. the
Beryl/Cobalt activation registry with the Base admin) on REVM 42, fed only by
Helios's ProofDB through a REVM 43->42 database bridge. Other OP Stack chains
keep op-revm; wasm builds refuse Base execution. The Base fork horizon refusal
stays the shipped default. Requires Rust 1.96 (base/base rust-version).
